# What the knowledge graph is FOR here: the code and the prose that explains it.
#
# WHY IMAGES ARE EXCLUDED, and it is not a size preference. graphify gives each
# image its OWN semantic chunk ("vision needs separate context"), and with no
# GEMINI_API_KEY set the host agent is the LLM -- so 4,869 frames would mean 4,869
# subagent dispatches. Those frames are match captures, compass glyphs and walk
# recordings: they are DATA the readers are measured against, not knowledge about
# how the system fits together. A graph of them answers no question anyone asks.
#
# Counted 2026-09-17 with graphify.detect:
#   2396  overnight/local_hand      hand crops
#   1068  overnight/drives          recorded walks
#    270  overnight/crawl
#    237  test_fixtures/harvest
#    209  test_fixtures/compass_glyphs
#    205  chains/route_user_1853
#   ----  4869 total, against 717 code files and 64 documents
#
# The named fixture directories stay listed individually rather than as *.jpg so a
# NEW image directory shows up in the next detect as an unexplained count, instead
# of being silently swallowed by a glob.
overnight/local_hand/
overnight/drives/
overnight/crawl/
overnight/refused_hands/
overnight/cycle_frames/
overnight/chain_frames/
overnight/*failframes*/
overnight/prompt_zone_frames/
overnight/census/
chains/
places/
demos/
explore/
screenshot_log/
hand_samples/
test_fixtures/
agent_progress/
Photos of ban screen missing cards/

